% Test: nine verses of an 1861 poem (public domain) under the tune "O Tannenbaum"; verse 6 has two extra
% lines in the poem, so it does not fit and is reported.
X:1
T:Maryland, My Maryland
C:Words: James Ryder Randall (1861)
C:Tune: Lauriger Horatius / O Tannenbaum
M:3/4
L:1/8
K:C
W:1. The despot's heel is on thy shore,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:His torch is at thy temple door,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Avenge the patriotic gore
W:That flecked the streets of Baltimore,
W:And be the battle queen of yore,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:2. Hark to an exiled son's appeal,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:My Mother State! to thee I kneel,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:For life or death, for woe or weal,
W:Thy peerless chivalry reveal,
W:And gird thy beauteous limbs with steel,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:3. Thou wilt not cower in the dust,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Thy beaming sword shall never rust,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Remember Carroll's sacred trust,
W:Remember Howard's warlike thrust,
W:And all thy slumberers with the just,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:4. Come! 'tis the red dawn of the day,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Come with thy panoplied array,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:With Ringgold's spirit for the fray,
W:With Watson's blood at Monterey,
W:With fearless Lowe and dashing May,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:5. Come! for thy shield is bright and strong,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Come! for thy dalliance does thee wrong,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Come to thine own anointed throng,
W:Stalking with Liberty along,
W:And sing thy dauntless slogan song,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:6. Dear Mother! burst the tyrant's chain,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Virginia should not call in vain,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:She meets her sisters on the plain –
W:Sic semper! 'tis the proud refrain
W:That baffles minions back amain,
W:Maryland! Arise in majesty again,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:7. I see the blush upon thy cheek,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:For thou wast ever bravely meek,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:But lo! there surges forth a shriek,
W:From hill to hill, from creek to creek,
W:Potomac calls to Chesapeake,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:8. Thou wilt not yield the Vandal toll,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Thou wilt not crook to his control,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:Better the fire upon thee roll,
W:Better the shot, the blade, the bowl,
W:Than crucifixion of the Soul,
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
W:
W:9. I hear the distant thunder-hum,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:The Old Line bugle, fife, and drum,
W:Maryland, my Maryland!
W:She is not dead, nor deaf, nor dumb –
W:Huzza! She spurns the Northern scum!
W:She breathes! She burns! She'll come! She'll come!
W:Maryland! My Maryland!
